Package: epiPortrait
Type: Package
Title: Multi-Dimensional Geometric Profiling of Epigenetic Landscapes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Ying", family = "ZHANG",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "zhangying@example.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0005-9644-7062")))
Description: epiPortrait is a computational framework for analyzing epigenetic
    signals (ChIP-seq, ATAC-seq, CUT&Tag) beyond simple intensity. It extracts
    four-dimensional geometric features (Width, Intensity, Height, Skewness)
    from genomic domains and employs multivariate statistical testing (MANOVA)
    to identify Shape Shift events where the physical conformation of the
    epigenetic landscape changes between conditions, even when raw read counts
    do not. The package provides a complete pipeline from consensus peak
    calling and portrait matrix construction through statistical testing,
    shape classification, annotation, enrichment, power analysis, and
    publication-ready visualizations.
